Z||000008||danny boy||03-26-2001||08:21 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by 88formula:<BR><B>Slowest is arguable but worst handling? What do you have that handles allot better than a fiero?<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><BR> You've never been in MY car. I know all Fieros aren't bad handlers,but mine is the exception.My moms Buick century handles better. My control arm bushings are very worn,still has stock shocks/struts(78K),I have about an inch of front suspension travel(2" drop? not quite Fiero Store!) and The rear tires are winter treads,the front don't match. Oh, and theres something BAD wrong with the steering rack. <BR>I paid 600 for it and after the Fiero Factory disaster I have 1500 in the whole car.I havent done anything but drive it since I bought it.Don't worry,I'm starting the building process now.<P>I'm all for the Carlisle thing.Email me!!!<BR>First Fiero-Although I'm the most boring host in the planet we all can get together here one weekend if you want to come down. I have a spare bedroom so you can even stay here.Just give me time to get all my car parts outta there...<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/PFF_sig_2.jpg"> ||||reg||1
